(* http://www.wolfram.com/nb *)

Notebook[{
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["p^+ integration", "Title"],
Cell["\[Vee] >> k >> \[CapitalLambda] > 0.  Integrate only needs the ordering \[Vee] > k + \[CapitalLambda] to pick the branch; the strong ordering is what you use afterwards to expand the answer.", "Text"],
Cell["$Assumptions = {a > 0, k > 0, \[CapitalLambda] > 0, \[Vee] > k + \[CapitalLambda]};\n\nres = Integrate[\n   Exp[-I a p/k] (A/(p + k) - B/p - 1/k),\n   {p, \[CapitalLambda], \[Vee] - k}]", "Input"],
Cell["Result:\n\n  A E^(I a) ( Ei[-I a \[Vee]/k] - Ei[-I a (k + \[CapitalLambda])/k] )\n   - B ( Ei[-I a (\[Vee] - k)/k] - Ei[-I a \[CapitalLambda]/k] )\n   + I ( E^(-I a \[CapitalLambda]/k) - E^(-I a (\[Vee] - k)/k) ) / a\n\nwith Ei = ExpIntegralEi.", "Text"],
Cell["Now the strong ordering, using  Ei[-I x] = EulerGamma + Log[x] - I Pi/2 + O[x]  for small x  and  Ei[-I X] -> -I Pi Sign[X]  for large |X|:", "Text"],
Cell["asy = -A Exp[I a] (ExpIntegralEi[-I a] + I Pi Sign[a])\n   - B (Log[k/(Abs[a] \[CapitalLambda])] - EulerGamma - I Pi Sign[a]/2)\n   + I (1 - Exp[-I a (\[Vee] - k)/k])/a", "Input"],
Cell["\[Vee] has dropped out of the A and B terms -- the phase, not the cutoff, regulates them.  The only cutoff dependence left is the single Log[k/(|a| \[CapitalLambda])] on the B term.  The last term keeps its boundary oscillation; at a -> 0 it would be -(\[Vee] - k - \[CapitalLambda])/k, i.e. linearly divergent, so the phase cannot be dropped there.", "Text"]
}, Open]]
},
WindowSize->{900, 750},
WindowMargins->Automatic,
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb"
]
